  "notes": "Standard Maithili (Bihar / Nepal Terai). One of 22 scheduled languages of India (added 2003). Traditional Tirhuta script; Devanagari used officially. Phonologically close to Bengali and Nepali. This spec reads ⟨ऩ⟩, ⟨ऱ⟩ and ⟨ऴ⟩ as their base letters ⟨न⟩ [n], ⟨र⟩ [r] and ⟨ल⟩ [l], because the inventory has no separate phoneme for them. This spec has no ⟨ळ⟩, so ⟨ऴ⟩ takes the value of ⟨ल⟩.",
  "quality": "research",
